{
  "id": "meditation-prep",
  "name": "Meditation prep / temporal session (both sides)",
  "category": "meditation",
  "evidence": "unverified",
  "fidelity": "construct",
  "dose": {"value": [10, 50], "unit": "mG", "plane": "unstated", "cite": "Murphy, measurement.htm"},
  "origin": "Project construct from phase 1 of Todd Murphy's Feelgood session; timing rules from his Shakti meditation advice",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "A project construct for use before meditation: the temporal half of Murphy's Feelgood session run on its own for 30 min, with the amygdala and hippocampal signals one after the other over both temporal lobes. Murphy's meditation advice names the two-phase Feelgood and Altered States sessions or the hippocampal signal on the right, and says to meditate 'an hour to 90 minutes later', never during the session.",
  "notes": "Murphy's meditation page names the two-phase Feelgood and Altered States sessions over both sides, or 'the hippocampal signals over only the right side' (shakti_meditation.htm, 'Enhancing Meditation with Shakti'). The vendor warns that stopping the Feelgood session in its first phase 'may leave you further from the goal of the session' (feelgood_consent.htm). This program is the project's own design: that temporal phase alone, on two coils per side (FT7, TP7, FT8, TP8; the site names are this project's reading). Each side has one positive and one negative coil, as in murphy-shakti8-feelgood-2phase-40min (vendor photos only). One pass: amygdala signal, 4 s of silence, hippocampal signal, 4 s of silence. Both are rebuilt: the vendor's files are not published. The amygdala signal is the project's rising sweep (6 to 30 Hz) with the published point duration and length (230 points of 3 ms; Ryczko 2002 p.1 [592]); its point values were never published as numbers. The hippocampal signal is a primed burst on 1-ms points: one pulse, then four pulses 170 ms later, three times in 0.74 s (after Tsang 2004 p.5 [1017]). The vendor says 'the standard signals have 3 msec points' (rapid_&_high_speed_signals.htm), so the point duration is this project's choice. The vendor's 10 to 50 mG carries no distance (measurement.htm, duds.htm); an independent meter read 0.1 to 1.0 uT RMS about 9 cm from the coils (Gendle 2012 p.11 [227]). This program's setting is the peak field 20 mm in front of each coil. No source tests a temporal-only session. Independent sham-controlled tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005, double-blind; Gendle & McGrath 2012, where the experimenter knew the condition). Aggression rose with continuous burst-firing (n = 4), not with 1 s every 4 s (Gillis 1993 p.2 [169]); stop if you notice irritability. No meditation or other mind machines during the session. Not for people with epilepsy, migraine, a psychiatric diagnosis or medication.",
  "setting": "No darkness or sensory deprivation needed; seated, eyes closed, relaxed but not meditating. Meditate 60-120 min after the session ends (Murphy: \"an hour to 90 minutes later\").",
  "schedule": "Weekly or every 72 h, never on consecutive days; several sessions may be needed before an effect is noticed. Series of six, then a 21-day break. For Murphy's lucid-dream series use murphy-shakti-lucid-dream-series-temporal, not this program.",
  "targets": ["left-amygdala", "right-amygdala", "left-hippocampus-body", "right-hippocampus-body"],
